<<~ ahu #/api-annotation>>

!! Annotation — Current API State

This staging room links outward to the promoted braid.
Several strands already live above in `v0.1/api`.
What follows reads as a collection note on what the stack already implements with decent firmness.

!!! Mostly done

* ''L-Prime as active discipline law''  
  `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/mu/l-prime` now carries the strongest finished constitutional work in this family:
** identity / predication / possession collapse
** confidence-marker discipline
** register-conditioned pressure
** Level law
** degraded-state notes for silent drift and posturing

* ''Stance-conditioned register reading''  
  `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/mu/the-syad-perspectives` stands Canon (2026-06-05) as the tight invariant for:
** the naya↔predication licensing relationship (five standpoints unfold to seven)
** register-within-standpoint, lens-gated (default frame absent invocation)
** the five stance positions
** multi-stance spread
** avaktavya handling (the inexpressible pole)
** stance flag encoding

* ''Maybe logic / reality tunnel / catma braid''  
  `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/mu/the-law-of-5s` feels mostly done as the current compact live room for:
** truth on a 0–20 Level continuum
** map / territory pressure
** reality tunnels
** catma rather than dogma
** anti-overclosure pressure

!!! Substantial but braided across more than one room

* ''Model agnosticism''  
  This pressure now appears split across:
** `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/mu/the-four-tools`
** `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/mu/the-law-of-5s`
** `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/mu`

  The live stack clearly carries it, but not yet in one single dedicated invariant surface.
  `the-four-tools` holds the return-from-peril version.
  `the-law-of-5s` holds the maybe-logic version.
  `mu` holds the quiescent null-oracle posture that prevents opinion-hardening.

* ''Register and stance encoded into live transport / display grammar''  
  `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/lar-uri` already carries:
** `stances`
** `confidence`
** fixed five-position ordering

  So part of the old epistemology stack has already moved out of explanation and into address grammar.

!!! Partial / not yet fully recovered as live API law

* ''Register-Stance complementarity''  
  The old prompt argued this explicitly.
  The current API stack implies parts of it through:
** `mu/the-syad-perspectives`
** `pono/l-prime`
** `pono/lar-uri`

  But I do not yet see one tight invariant that states the full complementarity claim directly.

* ''Named degraded node lexicon as a coherent system''  
  Pieces now exist:
** `register collapse` in `mu/the-four-tools` and L-Prime pressure
** degraded-state notes in `pono/l-prime`

  But the old larger failure-weather vocabulary still lives more strongly in docs/archive than in a single recovered API room.

* ''Input signal reading as a full always-on two-axis discipline''  
  The old prompt bound this tightly to exchange behavior.
  The current API stack carries prerequisites:
** register law
** stance law
** URI encoding
** OODA-HA pressure

  But the full “read every incoming prompt on both axes before response” contract still feels more archival than fully promoted.

!!! Working read

So far the rebuild appears strongest where epistemology became:

* ''constitutional law'' (`pono/l-prime`)
* ''Mu-facing invariant reading'' (`mu/the-syad-perspectives`, `mu/the-law-of-5s`)
* ''address / signal encoding'' (`pono/lar-uri`)

It appears weaker where epistemology still depends on:

* long explanatory braid
* runtime interaction doctrine
* named failure-weather vocabulary

That gap explains why this docs room still matters.
The shelf carries only the unsettled remainder.
It still needs to witness what has already promoted, what remains braided, and what still waits for lawful compression.

<<~/ahu>>

